WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.160
- So the President called a
meeting with Sidney Powell

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.780
and Rudy Giuliani, amongst others

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.180
to discuss Sidney Powell
becoming special counsel

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.820
to the White House in
charge of election fraud.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.673
Also at the meeting,

00:00:10.673 --> 00:00:11.910
they discussed issuing an executive order

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.410
to seize voting machines

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.620
and potentially using
the military to, I guess,

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.790
redo the election.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.530
So the President is in
full Leeroy Jenkins mode,

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.280
but there's good news and
bad news about Sidney Powell

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.160
as special counsel.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.100
Number one, this may

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.370
or may not be a Mueller-type
special counsel.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.060
It may just be a post
created at the White House

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.390
and as bonkers as that is,

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.270
National Security
Counselor Kel McClanahan,

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.230
who is also the lawyer
for Legal Eagle points out

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.840
that basically zero oversight,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.670
FOIA wouldn't apply until 2025

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.240
if they don't destroy the
records on the way out.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.840
But if she got a security clearance,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.010
she'd have to go through the
same pre-publication review

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.180
that John Bolton did.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.920
So Merry Christmas, everyone.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.270
But if you'd like some real holiday cheer,

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.260
check out this video I
did on all the laws broken

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.090
in "National Lampoon's
Christmas Vacation".

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.823
And I'll see you in court.

